# Intentionally present and effectively empty.
#
# GitHub Pages runs every commit through Jekyll by default, and Jekyll treats
# {{ }} and {% %} as template tags. A Jekyll build FAILS SILENTLY, and a failed
# build makes Pages keep serving the LAST SUCCESSFUL build for the WHOLE SITE.
# Symptom: the commit is correct on main, the live URL is frozen, and it looks
# like a cache problem but is not.
#
# This file disables Jekyll so files deploy verbatim. NEVER DELETE IT.
